==English==

===Etymology===
Unclear. Perhaps a corruption of ''dick'', or from the use of ''duck'' in sexual slang.<ref>Victoria de Rijke, ''Duck'' (2008), page 103, mentions some sexual slang senses of ''duck'' including as [dated?] US slang for 'gay' as in"watch your ass: there's duck dudes round here", ''duckpond'' as 'vagina', and ''duck butter''.</ref> Attested since at least 1973.<ref>Tom Dalzell, ''The Routledge Dictionary of Modern American Slang and Unconventional English'', Routledge (2018, {{ISBN|9781351765206}})</ref>

